<figure id="S6.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T2.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S6.T2.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Main results of our proposed Doc-Mix-trained D2I methods. The <span id="S6.T2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span> denotes the best performance, while the <span id="S6.T2.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underline</span> denotes the second best one. In the Qwen w/ GRPO, we evaluate the model with the deliberate reasoning, while in w/ GRPO<sup id="S6.T2.9.3" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S6.T2.9.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> we evaluate with the intuitive reasoning. <math id="S6.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\Delta}_{base}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta}_{base}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the improvement of D2I over Qwen2.5-VL-7B, while <math id="S6.T2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\Delta}_{grpo\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">†</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\Delta}_{grpo\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the improvement over Qwen2.5-VL-7B w/ GRPO<sup id="S6.T2.9.4" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S6.T2.9.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup>. <sup id="S6.T2.9.5" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S6.T2.9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">⋆</span></sup> denotes our re-implementation.</span></figcaption>
